# Two sibling nested methods of a factory read the same host formal through
# `node`; the returned method calls both. The copied context stages that
# formal once, at the one slot both readers address: (7 + 1) + (7 + 2) = 17.
# Exit 7 on the correct value; 81 is the program's own refusal.
fn: makeOuter (int: n) fn: () int
    fn: left () int
        return: node\n + 1
    fn: right () int
        return: node\n + 2
    fn: inner () int
        return: left() + right()
    return: inner
@: held makeOuter(7)
int: got held()
int: ok 7
if: got != 17
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
